it9308 bundles one thing that is not original work:

1. `vendor/usb/` - pyusb, BSD-3-Clause. Its licence is `vendor/usb/LICENSE`.

The bridge firmware image is **not** part of this repository: it is vendor material and is not
redistributed. The driver asks for it at run time (`--firmware`, `IT9308_FIRMWARE`, or a file beside
the package); `list` and `probe` do not need it.

`it9308/sequence.py` and `java/src/main/resources/it9308/sequence.bin` are the same protocol capture
(observed USB traffic), not firmware, and are part of this tree.

## Provenance marker

`it9308-pbcnx` is a visible provenance/attribution string in the Python and Java metadata (`--version`,
`It9308Device.PROVENANCE`). It is intended to make the origin searchable and to encourage the MIT notice to
travel with copies. It is **not** telemetry: it performs no network or device I/O, carries no user or device
identifier, and changes no protocol bytes.

